{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented and pushed: Gerrit change 1940 (commit ced46ae39b, Change-Id Ie98465f3d4c0a92c901593ad06b0c0a3433c13d9).\n\nSEAM: raw-input resolution (stays in `_config_sources.py`) vs the RP-04 below-seam OWNED RESOLVERS (move to the new `src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py`). The file already drew this boundary with four banner comments naming the RP-04 tickets d074 / 9515 / 1b07 + the reconciler JIRA family. Call graph is one-directional and narrow: no raw-input symbol names a resolver, and exactly ONE resolver body (`_snapshot_table`) reaches back.\n\nSIZES: 791 -> 403 (`_config_sources.py`) + 480 (`_config_resolvers.py`). Both inside the 200-500 target; 397 and 320 lines of headroom under the 800 cap. Neither is under 100.\n\nIMPORT SURFACE: byte-identical. `sorted(dir(rebar._config_sources))` and `sorted(dir(rebar.config))` compared against pre-split origin/main @ e278425d7a: 0 missing, 0 added, both modules.\n\nTWO-SIDED BINDING RESULT:\n- Side 1 (moved): zero string references to any of the 29 moved names anywhere in the tree. Nothing to break.\n- Side 2 (called by moved code): `_snapshot_table` resolves `user_config_path` / `_read_toml_table` / `_discover_project_config` through a lazy in-body `from rebar import _config_sources`, called as module attributes at call time. MUTATION-CHECKED: switching to eager import-time binding turns 3 binding tests + the acyclicity test + 3 seam-membership tests RED (7 failures). That is the exact Gerrit-1932 defect, and the new test file catches it.\n\nDOCS/ENV DRIFT: `docs/env-vars.md` DID need regenerating — 24 owning-file rows moved, and the non-literal-read citation moved from `_config_sources.py:612` to `_config_resolvers.py:301`. `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check` now exits clean. Also corrected one stale `<file>:<line>` prose citation of `_read_toml_table` (111-115 -> 153-159) in `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_user_guide_commands.py` — a docstring reference only; no assertion or behaviour touched, and no existing test was modified to make anything pass.\n\nCONFIG-OWNERSHIP SEAM: no config read crosses it. One composition root, two files: `_config_resolvers.py` added to `COMPOSITION_ROOT_BASENAMES` in `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` (classification is by basename). The gate exits 0. The parametrized held-out test at `tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py:190-196` is a per-seam pass test, not an exhaustive-set assertion, so it did not need changing; the new seam test asserts the membership instead.\n\nGATES: `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` -> `active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0` (no `_config_sources` symbol was baselined, so neither trap fired). `.github/module-size-limit.txt` and `.github/complexity-baseline.json` unmodified. `make lint` and `make typecheck` (mypy, 577 files) pass. WHOLE tree: `pytest tests --ignore=tests/external` -> 14738 passed, 58 skipped, 1 xfailed, exit 0 (includes tests/interfaces, where the first run caught a real env-registry staleness — `ruff format` had shifted the cited line by one after my first regeneration)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787193262666819001,"uuid":"b2405cca-9cf7-4456-93be-8ae548a7501c"}